        "created_at": "2015-06-10T02:10:22.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>My family is a fan of the Drury Inn chain, headquartered in St Louis. I haven't had a reason to look up prices recently, but they've got a nightly thing that happens around dinner time in which there's food out which could become a meal rather than just chips/cheese sauce, and guests of drinking age get two per night during the stay and serve breakfast in the morning. We've got two kids, so the money saved on meals makes up for any offset in the price for the room.</p>",
